WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:10.846
<v Maya Okafor>Alright, happy Friday everyone. Let’s get started—quick round of updates before we dive into the handbook stuff. Lukas, want to kick us off?</v>

00:00:11.137 --> 00:00:25.368
<v Lukas Brenner>Sure, thanks Maya. Not much from EMEA this week, just a couple of questions from folks in Poland about dental coverage, but nothing urgent. Oh, and I finally got the Zurich renewal docs, so we’re good there.</v>

00:00:26.431 --> 00:00:37.585
<v Priya Raman>APAC’s been pretty quiet too. I did get a ping from someone in India about the wellness stipend, but I just pointed them to the FAQ. Otherwise, all good.</v>

00:00:38.215 --> 00:00:46.676
<v Daniel Ferreira>Comp side, I’m still working through the mid-year review data. Should have the comp benchmarking ready for next week’s call. No blockers.</v>

00:00:47.284 --> 00:00:58.823
<v Tomás Rivera>Legal’s all clear. I did a quick review of the Zurich policy wording, nothing stands out as problematic. Happy to help if anything comes up in the policy changes today.</v>

00:01:00.125 --> 00:01:09.740
<v Maya Okafor>Awesome, thanks everyone. Oh, and I’ll be out next Friday, so Daniel will run the sync. Okay, let’s jump into the main item—Singapore handbook updates.</v>

00:01:10.876 --> 00:01:20.107
<v Maya Okafor>So, we’ve got three sections to review: Medical Insurance, Personal Accident, and the Questions bit. Lukas, can you walk us through the proposed changes?</v>

00:01:20.697 --> 00:01:35.697
<v Lukas Brenner>Yep. For Medical Insurance, we’re just clarifying that the IHP App has the most up-to-date panel list, not just the PDF. Also, adding a couple more features to the portal section, like the I-Health Palace marketplace and hotline info.</v>

00:01:36.299 --> 00:01:45.915
<v Priya Raman>Wait, Lukas, on the IHP App—do we need to mention anywhere that people should check both the app and the PDF, or just the app?</v>

00:01:46.646 --> 00:01:57.030
<v Lukas Brenner>Good question. I think we should say the app is the most current, but keep the PDF link for reference. That’s what I put in the draft.</v>

00:01:57.753 --> 00:02:05.446
<v Maya Okafor>Yeah, I like that. It’s clearer for folks who are used to the PDF but nudges them to the app.</v>

00:02:06.030 --> 00:02:10.645
<v Daniel Ferreira>Agreed. And the new features—are those live now? Like the marketplace thing?</v>

00:02:11.011 --> 00:02:17.165
<v Lukas Brenner>Yes, they launched it last month. I double-checked with IHP support, so it’s safe to include.</v>

00:02:17.911 --> 00:02:27.142
<v Tomás Rivera>Just a quick legal note: the hotline number, is that the same as in the contract? We don’t want to publish the wrong one.</v>

00:02:28.565 --> 00:02:33.180
<v Lukas Brenner>Yep, it matches. I cross-referenced the latest IHP guide and our contract.</v>

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:38.876
<v Maya Okafor>Perfect. Okay, moving on—Personal Accident Insurance. Lukas, can you summarize the change?</v>

00:02:40.249 --> 00:02:52.173
<v Lukas Brenner>Sure. We’re updating the benefit to 36 times basic monthly salary, with a min of $500k and max $3 million. Also, updating the links to the new policy docs and overview.</v>

00:02:53.173 --> 00:03:01.634
<v Priya Raman>Is the 36x formula standard? Just want to make sure we’re not confusing people who are used to seeing a flat number.</v>

00:03:02.226 --> 00:03:08.379
<v Daniel Ferreira>Yeah, it’s pretty standard for group policies in Singapore. The min and max should help clarify.</v>

00:03:09.292 --> 00:03:17.369
<v Tomás Rivera>From a legal perspective, as long as we specify the min and max, and link to the full policy, we’re covered.</v>

00:03:17.569 --> 00:03:21.031
<v Maya Okafor>Alright, sounds good. Any other concerns on this one?</v>

00:03:21.604 --> 00:03:23.104
<v Priya Raman>Nope, I’m good.</v>

00:03:23.863 --> 00:03:25.363
<v Lukas Brenner>All clear here.</v>

00:03:26.316 --> 00:03:29.393
<v Maya Okafor>Okay, last one—the Questions section. Lukas, what’s changing?</v>

00:03:30.445 --> 00:03:40.060
<v Lukas Brenner>We’re updating the claims support contact to Pacific Prime, since they’re our new broker. Added their email and phone, and clarified they handle escalations too.</v>

00:03:40.864 --> 00:03:47.018
<v Daniel Ferreira>Do we need to keep the Willis Towers Watson email, or is that totally replaced now?</v>

00:03:47.793 --> 00:03:53.178
<v Lukas Brenner>It’s replaced. Pacific Prime handles everything now, so we can remove the old info.</v>

00:03:53.655 --> 00:03:59.809
<v Tomás Rivera>Just make sure the Pacific Prime contacts are correct. I’ve seen a couple versions floating around.</v>

00:04:00.624 --> 00:04:05.624
<v Lukas Brenner>I confirmed with their team this morning, so these are the right ones.</v>

00:04:06.996 --> 00:04:10.458
<v Maya Okafor>Great. Any other questions or concerns before we decide?</v>

00:04:11.692 --> 00:04:13.615
<v Priya Raman>Nope, looks good to me.</v>

00:04:14.036 --> 00:04:15.536
<v Daniel Ferreira>All good.</v>

00:04:15.846 --> 00:04:17.385
<v Tomás Rivera>No issues from legal.</v>

00:04:18.255 --> 00:04:27.870
<v Maya Okafor>Alright, so to summarize: we’re approving all three handbook changes as drafted. Lukas, can you update the handbook page by the end of the month?</v>

00:04:28.893 --> 00:04:34.278
<v Lukas Brenner>Yep, I’ll get those changes in and ping the team for review before publishing.</v>

00:04:34.913 --> 00:04:50.683
<v Maya Okafor>Awesome, thanks. Last thing—quick unrelated item. We got the pulse survey results back, and there’s some feedback about the onboarding experience. Daniel, can you take a look and maybe draft a couple of action items for us to discuss next week?</v>

00:04:51.947 --> 00:05:01.177
<v Daniel Ferreira>Sure, I’ll review the results and put together some suggestions. Should I share them in Slack or just bring them to the next sync?</v>

00:05:02.354 --> 00:05:05.046
<v Maya Okafor>Slack’s fine, just tag the group. Thanks!</v>

00:05:06.121 --> 00:05:10.736
<v Priya Raman>Oh, and Maya, are we still planning the team offsite for September?</v>

00:05:11.228 --> 00:05:16.997
<v Maya Okafor>Yes, but I’ll send a poll next week to lock in dates. More to come.</v>

00:05:17.456 --> 00:05:18.995
<v Tomás Rivera>Looking forward to it!</v>

00:05:19.226 --> 00:05:22.303
<v Lukas Brenner>Same here. Okay, anything else before we wrap?</v>

00:05:22.822 --> 00:05:25.899
<v Maya Okafor>Nope, that’s it. Thanks everyone—have a great weekend!</v>

00:05:26.716 --> 00:05:28.216
<v Priya Raman>Thanks, you too!</v>

00:05:29.521 --> 00:05:31.021
<v Daniel Ferreira>Bye all!</v>

00:05:31.316 --> 00:05:32.816
<v Tomás Rivera>Take care, everyone.</v>

00:05:33.554 --> 00:05:35.054
<v Lukas Brenner>Bye!</v>
